From 00281ea4342ea6c1b79eef12603781d6ec44c589 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:07:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: make an UNREGISTERED measured win refuse the
 update path

WI-1688. R2-CLOSURE-REPORT section 6 named this as the honest weak point of that pass: nothing forced a lane to REGISTER a win it landed. The manifest could be complete and still true while a measured mechanism landed beside it, guarding nothing. The refusal is now inside the existing chokepoint - validate_protected_wins gains strict registration, check calls validate, bump leg 1b calls check. No parallel updater was invented and there is no skip flag.

protected-win-baseline.json is the dated, sha-pinned disposition ledger for the 24 measured-effect commits that had ALREADY landed when the gate was switched on. It exists because the only two alternatives are both bad: fail on all 24 (a gate nobody can pass is a gate somebody switches off), or file the real wins under a soft reason so the gate goes quiet - which is the discard the President's mandate forbids, wearing a receipt. Eight rows carry REGISTRATION OWED and name the win they are owed for; they are not closed and not dismissed. The ledger is closed to new shas: a new win is registered.

Classifier defect found BY these tests and fixed here: NO_EFFECT_PREFIXES contained a bare dash tested as a PREFIX, so 'Measured-effect: -12.79% per dispatch' classified as NO EFFECT. Every speedup written as a negative delta - the most common shape a win takes on this fork - was invisible to discovery. The dash is an exact match now (NO_EFFECT_EXACT) and a regression test pins it.

discover keeps an explicit informational mode (--all lists baseline rows and dispositions) so the ledger cannot rot unseen; the default output is exactly the set that refuses an update, so the report and the gate can never disagree.

Tests 14 to 22, stdlib only. New fail-closed negatives: an unregistered measured win fails validate; refuses the preflight; refuses bump BEFORE it replays (asserted by replacing _replay with a raiser, because a return code alone would pass even if the refusal came after a replay). New must-not-fire cases: a registered win passes, a baselined win passes, and documentation/tooling/unmeasured trailers do not false-positive - a noisy fail-closed gate is how a skip flag gets added.

LIVE two-halves receipt on REAL fork history, not fixtures (F-043): lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/rank3-r10/77-strict-registration-LIVE.txt - GREEN 0 problems with the baseline in place, RED 24 problems with it absent. UPDATE-RUNBOOK 4.1c step 7 rewritten from advice to mechanism: exact commands, a semantics table, both honest ways to close a row, and the classifier trap recorded.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: tooling and documentation only; no engine behaviour changed and no shipped default moved
WI: WI-1688
Lane: lane-209
